ol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>652</fpage>&#x02013;662.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16633346</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Zheng, S.G., J.H. Wang, J.D. Gray, H. Soucier, and D.A. Horwitz. <year>2004</year>. Natural and induced CD4&#x0002b;CD25&#x0002b; cells educate CD4&#x0002b;CD25&#x02212; cells to develop suppressive activity: the role of IL-2, TGF-beta, and IL-10. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>172</volume>:<fpage>5213</fpage>&#x02013;5221.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15100259</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fantini, M.C., C. Becker, G. Monteleone, F. Pallone, P.R. Galle, and M.F. Neurath. <year>2004</year>. Cutting edge: TGF-beta induces a regulatory phenotype in CD4&#x0002b;CD25&#x02212; T cells through Foxp3 induction and down-regulation of Smad7. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>172</volume>:<fpage>5149</fpage>&#x02013;5153.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15100250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Karim, M., C.I. Kingsley, A.R. Bushell, B.S. Sawitzki, and K.J. Wood. <year>2004</year>. Alloantigen-induced CD25&#x0002b;CD4&#x0002b; regulatory T cells can develop in vivo from CD25&#x02212;CD4&#x0002b; precursors in a thymus-independent process. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>172</volume>:<fpage>923</fpage>&#x02013;928.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14707064</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fontenot, J.D., J.P. Rasmussen, L.M. Williams, J.L. Dooley, A.G. Farr, and A.Y. Rudensky. <year>2005</year>. Regulatory T cell lineage specification by the forkhead transcription factor foxp3. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>22</volume>:<fpage>329</fpage>&#x02013;341.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15780990</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Smith, T.J., L.A. Ducharme, S.K. Sh